@BE_HostAddress = https://localhost:7089
@accessToken = PASTE_LOGIN_TOKEN_HERE

### Create an account first. Example values do not identify a pre-created account.
POST {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com",
  "password": "MarkoTest2026!",
  "gender": "Male"
}

### Sign in, then copy token from the JSON response into accessToken above.
POST {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marko@example.com",
  "password": "MarkoTest2026!"
}

### List your workouts. Authorization header requires Bearer; Swagger's dialog adds it itself.
GET {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/trainings?page=1&pageSize=10&sortBy=trainingDate&sortDirection=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Create a workout.
POST {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/trainings
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exerciseType": "Strength",
  "durationMinutes": 45,
  "calories": 250,
  "intensity": 7,
  "fatigue": 5,
  "trainingDate": "2026-10-27T18:00:00",
  "notes": "Upper body workout"
}

### Monthly statistics.
GET {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/trainings/month?year=2026&month=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Requires the Admin role. User accounts receive 403.
GET {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/admin/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh requires a client that stores and sends the cookie from login.
# In Swagger on the same HTTPS host, the browser handles the HttpOnly cookie automatically.
POST {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh

### Revoke the refresh cookie session. Existing JWTs last until expiry.
POST {{BE_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
